    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d247">

                <pb facs="0227" n="177" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg177"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/397</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Advisory Commission of Railway
                        Experts to Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-05-21T07:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 21, 1918, 7
                                a.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 12.40 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Chinese Eastern asking if embargo at Manchuria Station can not be raised at once
                    enough to enable it to supply their workers who are repairing damaged railway
                    west and restoring transportation. I think they have a feeling that in keeping
                    embargo the Allies are not neutral towards them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
